# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest, and reproduces issue #4700's second half: the
# purge's evidence is shard-wide (ShardRootState.LeafClearsBegun), so it also
# names a leaf the purge never reached. That leaf's row was lost to a fault and
# its pin retired; the GC trimmed past it; recovery re-creates it empty, and it
# silently loses writes nobody deleted. The base marks only the leaf the purge
# reached. The depth-15 trace of the #4433 confirmation pass.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestShardWidePurgeMarker
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a shard-wide purge marker lets recovery re-create a leaf the purge never reached
PERTURBS: MarkPurge

--- FIND
    /\ purgeRec' = [purgeRec EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the marker names every leaf of the shard.
    /\ purgeRec' = [k \in Leaves |-> TRUE]
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot or a leaf row.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row and the snapshot both vanish: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END